3.8.1 to 3.8.3 Health certificate registration, validation, and revocation linked to professional credentials&#xD;
</documentation>
    </element>
    <element xsi:type="archimate:DataObject" name="Facility Registry" id="id-448772e005ac433690808dff1bae3163">
      <documentation>Facility Registry (health facilities metadata system): Maintains metadata about health facilities such as name, type, ownership, location, services offered, operational status, identifiers, and contact details. Supplies metadata on source facilities contributing data; supports data provenance and verification.&#xD;
&#xD;
Facility Registry (Health Facilities Metadata System)&#xD;
2.1.2 Enrolment of persons in facility-based clinical plans&#xD;
2.2.1 to 2.2.3 Facility-linked clinical record storage&#xD;
2.4 Telemedicine (2.4.1 to 2.4.4) facility location and infrastructure metadata&#xD;
2.5 Healthcare provider communication (2.5.1 to 2.5.4) facility-based coordination&#xD;
2.6 Referral coordination (2.6.1 to 2.6.3) inter-facility referral tracking&#xD;
2.7 Scheduling and activity planning (2.7.1 to 2.7.2) service availability at facilities&#xD;
2.10 Laboratory and diagnostics imaging (2.10.1 to 2.10.4) identifies testing and reporting facilities&#xD;
2.11 Healthcare provider financial transactions (2.11.1 to 2.11.2) facility-based reimbursements and payments&#xD;
3.7.1 List health facilities and related information&#xD;
3.7.2 Assess health facilities&#xD;
</documentation>
    </element>
    <element xsi:type="archimate:DataObject" name="Terminology Server" id="id-29a19c67c2304566bc623f8948303c27">
      <documentation>Terminology Server (SNOMED/ICD/LOINC server). Manages metadata describing code systems, value sets, and concept mappings used to standardize health data semantics. Ensures standard clinical terminology, enabling consistent and verifiable record content.&#xD;
&#xD;
Terminology Server (SNOMED, ICD, LOINC, or Local Metadata Server)&#xD;
2.2 Person-centred health records (2.2.1 to 2.2.4) coded diagnoses and observations&#xD;
2.3 Decision support (2.3.1 to 2.3.3) protocol and rule definitions use coded data&#xD;
2.4 Telemedicine (2.4.3) standardized data exchange formats&#xD;
2.5 Communication (2.5.3 to 2.5.6) use of consistent terminology in reports&#xD;
2.9 Prescription and medication management (2.9.1 to 2.9.3) coded medicines and adverse events&#xD;
2.10 Laboratory and diagnostics (2.10.1 to 2.10.4) LOINC or SNOMED codes for tests&#xD;
2.11 Financial transactions (2.11.1 to 2.11.2) standardized service and billing codes&#xD;
3.8.1 to 3.8.3 Health certificate types and validation statuses standardized by terminology codes</documentation>
    </element>
    <element xsi:type="archimate:DataObject" name="Product Catalogue" id="id-0cbdfd18c0a24d7e817e78c50cff5dc8">
      <documentation>Product Catalogue: Standardizes metadata on medications and services to support consistent longitudinal tracking.</documentation>
    </element>
    <element xsi:type="archimate:ApplicationComponent" name="Knowledge Base Engine" id="id-7902b43e775944aeb048890217d16983">
      <documentation>Knowledge Base Engine: A component that stores and processes medical protocols, clinical guidelines, and best practices. It's the &quot;brain&quot; of the DDSS.</documentation>
    </element>
    <element xsi:type="archimate:ApplicationComponent" name="Shared Health Record" id="id-4aa283f7a18b4a8dbec70095cb11af3c">
      <documentation>Shared Health Record:&#xD;
for Care Plan Management (e.g. FHIR CarePlan/Goal/Task resources)&#xD;
for Discharge Summary (FHIR Composition/DocumentReference/Bundle)&#xD;
for Referral &amp; Transfer Module (FHIR ServiceRequest, Encounter, CarePlan)&#xD;
FHIR-based: Encounter, Observation, Condition, CarePlan, Goal, Task, EpisodeOfCare)</documentation>
    </element>
    <element xsi:type="archimate:ApplicationComponent" name="Interoperability Layer" id="id-5cff525357f941828baee33eb25dc6d1">
      <documentation>Interoperability Layer: This component uses interoperability standards (e.g., HL7, FHIR) to connect to various Electronic Health Records (EHRs) and other health information systems to gather patient data.</documentation>
    </element>
    <element xsi:type="archimate:ApplicationComponent" name="Electronic Medical Record" id="id-e4408dd2c2a043c59c93fdb46a389c88">
      <documentation>Electronic Medical Record: This is the front-end that healthcare workers interact with, providing a unified dashboard for patient history, protocols, and decision support alerts.</documentation>
    </element>
    <element xsi:type="archimate:ApplicationComponent" name="Access Control and Authentication Component" id="id-df1bd888ccfa4bcd9f24e659cd90db68">
      <documentation>Access Control and Authentication Component: Ensures that only authorized personnel can access sensitive patient information, adhering to privacy regulations.</documentation>
    </element>
    <element xsi:type="archimate:ApplicationService" name="Clinical Decision Support Service" id="id-d7d2610e083943e694754488442a0252">
      <documentation>Clinical Decision Support Service: This service provides real-time guidance based on patient data and up-to-date medical protocols.</documentation>
    </element>
    <element xsi:type="archimate:ApplicationService" name="Patient History Aggregation Service" id="id-ff8a651ec88942ff88909be2442f9205">
      <documentation>Patient History Aggregation Service: This service consolidates patient records from various sources (e.g., labs, clinics, hospitals) into a single, unified view.</documentation>
    </element>
    <element xsi:type="archimate:ApplicationService" name="Care Protocol Management Service" id="id-350708dd1a414a61863ed4900b97b5ed">
      <documentation>Care Protocol Management Service: This service manages, updates, and distributes the latest evidence-based care protocols to all connected healthcare facilities.</documentation>
    </element>
    <element xsi:type="archimate:ApplicationService" name="Care Coordination and Task Assignment Service" id="id-819f7bd07c3845cbb8502a1ac907479f">
      <documentation>Care Coordination and Task Assignment Service: This service facilitates the referral of patients and the delegation of tasks between different health workers and facilities.</documentation>
    </element>
